Okay, so Bob isn't a good name for a Valkyrie- I'm too
lazy to change the name in my environment variable...

Anyway, I am living proof that occasionally, no matter how
stupid you are, the RNG decides that you are going to 
ascend, and won't take no for an answer.

An early wand of wishing made me overconfident.  It netted
me 2 blessed scrolls of charging, silver dragon scale mail,
speed boots, and a magic marker.  I used a lot of marker
charges on scrolls of identify, which were not plentiful
this game (I hadn't found one after clearing Sokoban and
the Mines...).  At -18 AC, Lord Surtur was a pushover.
My ring of conflict helped me clear out Fort Ludios and
the Castle with relative ease as well.  At that point,
I got too confident, using all of my wishes for nice 
pieces of armor (tshirt, gauntlets of power, etc.), and
magic markers to enchant my armor, bringing me to AC -47.

I foolishly used my last marker charges on the scrolls of
gold detection that I just KNEW I was going to need soon.
Unfortunately, since I'm posting this, I obviously won't
learn from my mistake.  I continued on and cleared out
the named demons quite easily, found the square, marked it,
etc.  When I went after Rodney, I froze the water outside
of his little room, instead of using my ring of levitation
for some reason.  When he came out to fight me, something
shot fire into the water and melted the ice, and I
accidently stepped in it.  I'm guessing this is what happened
to 3 of my 4 scrolls of gold detection.  I figured at this
point I might as well try it without these, but I was
expecting disappointment.

On the way up, the mysterious force was very kind to me
for once- only threw me back a level once, and back away
from the stairs (but on the same level) 4 or 5 times.
Rodney appeared several times, and the wands of death that
the RNG left me kept missing him for some reason, but
eventually I got past him.

The planes were, uh, interesting compared to my past 
ascensions- I've never done most of the levels without 
scrolls to find the portals.  I got really lucky on 
Earth- I dug straight up, and saw a monster run into
it right away.  Air also worked out quite easily- I just
ran to the right, and hardly even got touched- none of
the elementals ever even got next to me.  Something triggered
the portal there too.  I started searching around on the
fire plane, and was having no luck, and then fell in the
lava.  I got tired of that, and decided to risk water without
the scroll.  Good choice- the damn portal was all the way
up in the upper left corner.  It would have taken an
eternity to get there.  I just wandered around on the water
plane for awhile, and the portal showed up there for me too.

At this point I felt very lucky, and figured that with my
huge stash of wands, my +7 Grayswandir, and just a tiny
bit of luck, I should be okay.  Of course, it took me
three tries to find the right altar.  Dancing around the
little a's and the big A's is becoming an art.

